mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Concepts and Significance of Medical Psychology; Concept of Health; Key Features of the Bio-Psycho-Social Medical Model; Concept of Stress, Fundamental Processes, Stress Responses, and Stress-Related Disorders; Patient Role, Doctor-Patient Relationship, Illness Experience, and Concept of Compliance; Basic Techniques of Doctor-Patient Communication; Concept, Scope, and Pathogenesis of Psychophysiological Disorders; Common Psychosomatic Diseases and Prevention Principles; Normal Sleep and Sleep Structure; Diagnosis and Treatment of Insomnia;Diagnosis and treatment of anorexia nervosa and bulimia nervosa; diagnostic and treatment principles for somatic symptom disorders and related conditions, clinical interview techniques; definition and risk assessment of suicide, suicide prevention; concepts of crisis and crisis intervention; fundamental principles and requirements of psychological measurement; definition, core elements, indications, and contraindications of psychotherapy; basic concepts and theories of behavioral therapy and cognitive therapy; definition and process of medical psychological counseling.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
